  "body": "As discussed in #289 the current setup can be confusing. This is what I think we should do:\r\n\r\n> I think I prefer equating string and JavaScript string, defining scalar value string and ASCII string as subsets, and then have code unit length and code point length. One of code unit length or code point length should also be called length, but which would really depend on usage.\r\n\r\nA reasonable start might be to do the above and keep both lengths we have today around as aliases for code unit length and code point length until we know which one to deprecate and remove. (Or perhaps we should favor neither and try to remove both shorthands.)\r\n\r\ncc @andreubotella",
